From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:23:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: Check subresource integrity before handing the response
 over

Main fetch handed the body of a request with integrity metadata over to
the consumer while reading it for the integrity check, before
`process_response`, and only then replaced the response with a network
error if the body did not match. So the consumer got the bytes of a body
that failed its check, and got them before the response.

Step 23 of main fetch fully reads the body first, and hands the response
over with those bytes only if they match the metadata; a null body fails
the check. Do that: read the whole body, check it, and hand over either the
response with the verified bytes, as one chunk, or a network error, through
the same handover as every other response. This also changes:

- An opaque or opaque-redirect response, whose body is null, now fails any
  integrity check without being read, even when the metadata does not
  parse; so does a null body status.
- A body that fails while it is read keeps its own network error and the
  response's timing, as without integrity metadata, instead of becoming an
  integrity failure.
- Devtools gets the body of a checked response after the response, and
  never gets the body of one that fails the check.

Validation: `./mach test-unit -p servo-net`: 497 tests pass. Against the previous patch, these new tests fail: `test_body_that_fails_its_integrity_check_is_not_delivered`, `test_body_cut_short_is_not_delivered_for_an_integrity_check` and `test_body_that_passes_its_integrity_check_is_delivered_after_the_response` (the target sees the body before the response), `test_synchronous_fetch_delivers_a_checked_body_after_the_response` (likewise for a synchronous fetch) and `test_opaque_response_fails_any_integrity_check` (an opaque response with metadata that does not parse is delivered); `test_null_body_fails_its_integrity_check` and `test_body_that_fails_to_decode_is_not_delivered_for_an_integrity_check` pass on both.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote this patch and its tests following docs/fetch-body-stream-plan-2026-10-22.md in the workspace, and applied an independent review's findings)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
